      "side": 1,
      "message": "`has_pending_bios_job()` reports \"no pending job\" for reads it could not perform, so the poll exits on the first iteration in exactly the case the comment above promises to wait through. `get_job_queue()` never checks `_response.status` (`badfish.py:529-534`), so a 503 or an HTML error body yields `[]`; a job GET returning None or non-200 is logged as \"skipping\" (`badfish.py:1012-1015`); an unparsable body likewise. The new `except` only catches the transport failures that raise `BadfishException`. Executed proof: with the jobs collection answering 503, `change_boot()` returns True after one GET and zero sleeps, while a readable queue with a Running job polls until it clears. Suggest returning None (or raising) for an unreadable read and treating None as keep waiting, the way `standard.py:372-380` does for BootMode. A 200 body that parses to a non-object also raises `AttributeError` from `data.get`, which escapes this `except`.",
